[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Hungarian Opening"]
[Variation "Hungarian Opening: King's Indian Attack Formation"]
[ECO "A00"]
[Character "solid,positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "qgd-setup"]
[Kind "sideline"]

1. g3 d5 { Takes the centre. White is planning a quiet fianchetto, so Black can set up calmly. }
2. Bg2 Nf6 { Develops and controls e4. The bishop on g2 hits d5, but that pawn is well guarded. }
3. Nf3 ( 3. c4 e6 4. Nf3 Be7 5. O-O O-O 6. b3 c5 7. Bb2 Nc6 ) 3... e6 { Backs up d5 and frees the bishop. The same setup works against every move order. }
4. O-O Be7 5. d3 O-O 6. Nbd2 c5 { Takes space on the queenside and prepares ...Nc6; the centre can wait. }
7. e4 Nc6 { Develops the last knight. If White takes on d5, Black recaptures and the pieces get active. } *
